				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/nahyesq" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5128230); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5128230&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608969260" alt="nahyesq" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5128230)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/nahyesq" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5128230); return false;" >nahyesq</a></span> <span class="odate time_1608966103 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">26 Dec 2020 07:01</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-89000/help:ideas-critique">Writing Help / Help: Ideas Critique</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13960067/a-thousand-door-seeking-greenlight">A Thousand Door (Seeking Greenlight)</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4853905">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre:</strong> Horror, Exploration, Ambiance</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout</strong>: Standard SCP Article with Explorations Logs towards the &quot;doors&quot;</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> it revolves around a building called Lawang Sewu, a colonial-era building that has a thousand doors because it really does have lots of doors in it. Every door has its own theme about Colonialism History, the upper place or the ground floor is accessible by a tourist, but the underground section of the floor is forbidden by the public, and the whole building itself should be monitored and staffed with Foundation Guards.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> The narrative will focus on the exploration logs about these &quot;doors&quot; that are in the underground, at first it will be a normal abandoned underground room with an 1800-1900s theme, as the exploration goes deeper, it will get an even weirder and darker theme of the place itself, some of it may cause cognitive disturbances, and some may have an entity that is hostile and non-hostile. The Exploration team must explore the room to progress further into another room, the room itself appears to be not in order which results in every room they encounter is randomized every time they started the exploration.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> Every room has its own theme, it tells how dark and cruel the colonization was. Tourists on the upper floor may see that colonization improved the country by a lot but in the underground, it tells the horrifying experience of being dictated by the upper echelon of that time. Tortured, discriminated, killed, etc by the colony. The Room expresses how the people back then were mistreated, some of the entities in the room being hostile because of it. The Foundation is still exploring the underground to know what really happened.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> I may add exploration logs also with some interviews with a non-hostile entity in the room to get a grasp of what does this room feels and its entity around it.</p>

							</div>

