<p>I actually had a line about that in an older version of the skip! Originally there was a much more complicated calculation of how much containment damage the anomaly did — the first time's calculation was a September's worth of days times a set number, the next time's was an October's worth of days, so on and so forth — and whether or not it honoured leap years was actually going to matter, because there'd be one extra day when February rolled around and that would make a difference between near-total failure and total failure.</p>
<p>I didn't include any of that, because it was TOO FUCKING COMPLICATED lol</p>
<p>But yes, to answer the question you actually asked, the anomaly happens on September 8 no matter how many days there are in February. Because, luckily, it's magic and a teeny tiny bit sentient.</p>

