<p>I have to say the core concept is well trod, the trope of something showing death and then trying to avoid it&#8230;</p>
<p>BUT, I think if you focus on the personal narrative of the researcher as you've proposed (make it a personal story about the fear of mortality, of getting older) then I think you have the core of a decent article. &quot;<em>They become obsessed with avoiding death using the laptop and eventually go too far and have to face the consequences of never dying, but not really living.</em>&quot; This is what you need to focus on.</p>
<p>So don't spend alot of time on the anomaly, its simple enough, get to the meat as soon as you can.</p>
<p>That's my advice, here's a <strong><span style="color: green">GREENLIGHT</span></strong></p>

